{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2022,3,29]],"date-time":"2022-03-29T21:48:47Z","timestamp":1648590527468},"reference-count":11,"publisher":"World Scientific Pub Co Pte Lt","issue":"08","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["Int. J. Theor. Appl. Finan."],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2015,12]]},"abstract":"<jats:p> A log-normal random walk with parameters that are functions of market stress naturally accounts for volatility clustering and fat-tailed return distributions. Fitting this model to a stock and a bond index we find no evidence of significant misspecification despite the fact that the model has no adjustable parameters. This model can be interpreted as a stochastic volatility model without latent variables. We obtain a closed-form expression for the Value at Risk (VaR) that accommodates returns of any magnitude and discuss several other applications. </jats:p>","DOI":"10.1142/s0219024915500545","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2015,11,20]],"date-time":"2015-11-20T12:02:41Z","timestamp":1448020961000},"page":"1550054","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":1,"title":["THE STRESS-DEPENDENT RANDOM WALK"],"prefix":"10.1142","volume":"18","author":[{"given":"MARTIN","family":"GREMM","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Pivot Point Advisors, LLC, 5959 West Loop South, Suite 333, Bellaire, TX 77401, USA"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"219","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2015,12,22]]},"reference":[{"key":"S0219024915500545BIB001","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016/0304-4076(86)90063-1"},{"key":"S0219024915500545BIB002","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.2307/1913889"},{"key":"S0219024915500545BIB003","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1111/1468-0262.00164"},{"key":"S0219024915500545BIB004","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1111/1540-6261.00566"},{"key":"S0